    "facts": [
      {
        "evidence_id": "S1",
        "en": "The checkAlreadyExpired function checks if a key has expired by comparing the key's expiration time with the current time. It also checks if the server is in a master mode and if the loading process is complete. This function supports the idea that a key should not be deleted immediately after expiration, but instead be added to the database with an expired expiration time and wait for an explicit delete from the master.",
        "pt-br": "A fun\u00e7\u00e3o checkAlreadyExpired verifica se uma chave expirou comparando o tempo de expira\u00e7\u00e3o da chave com o tempo atual. Al\u00e9m disso, verifica se o servidor est\u00e1 em modo mestre e se o processo de carregamento est\u00e1 completo. Essa fun\u00e7\u00e3o apoia a ideia de que uma chave n\u00e3o deve ser apagada imediatamente ap\u00f3s a expira\u00e7\u00e3o, mas sim ser adicionada \u00e0 base de dados com um tempo de expira\u00e7\u00e3o expirado e esperar por uma apaga\u00e7\u00e3o expl\u00edcita do mestre. "
      }
    ],
    "selected_evidence": {
      "S1": {
        "path": "src/expire.c",
        "line": 668,
        "quote": "int checkAlreadyExpired(long long when) {\n    /* EXPIRE with negative TTL, or EXPIREAT with a timestamp into the past\n     * should never be executed as a DEL when load the AOF or in the context\n     * of a slave instance.\n     *\n     * Instead we add the already expired key to the database with expire time\n     * (possibly in the past) and wait for an explicit DEL from the master. */\n    if (server.current_client && server.current_client->flags & CLIENT_MASTER) return 0;\n    return (when <= commandTimeSnapshot() && !server.loading && !server.masterhost);\n}\n",
        "complete_unit": true,
        "symbol": "checkAlreadyExpired",
        "enclosing_impl_hint": null,
        "qualified_symbol": "checkAlreadyExpired",
        "preparation": "explicit complete definition-layout range; not a language/semantic or runtime verifier"
      }
    },
